        <div class="prose col">
          <p>One downside of where I live: no fiber. T-Mobile Home Internet puts me behind CGNAT, with <b>no public IPv4</b> and no stable IPv6 &mdash; so nothing on the internet can reach my LAN directly. A couple of cheap cloud VPS solve it: they give me public IP addresses that route inbound traffic to my services. They route; they don't compute. Everything real still runs at home.</p>
